---
import Monument from './Monument.astro';
import { site } from '../consts';
---

<div class="intro">
  <Monument backdrop />

  <div class="column intro__body">
    <div class="title-row">
      <span class="title-row__mark">
        <img src="/mark.svg" alt="" width="44" height="44" />
      </span>
      <h1>{site.fullName}</h1>
    </div>

    <p>
      <a href={site.axiomsSsccs}>SSCCS</a> is an open-source computing systems initiative that
      replaces the sequential, instruction-centric model with a geometric{' '}
      <a href={`${site.whitepaperHtml}#observation-and-projection`}>observation-driven</a> model:
      spatial computation is the collapse of structured potential across a coordinate space composed
      of immutable{' '}
      <a href={`${site.whitepaperHtml}#definition-of-primitives`}>
        Segments, Scheme and dynamic Fields
      </a>{' '}
      composition. Parallelism and verifiability emerge from the structure itself, with near-linear
      scalability and energy efficiency as consequences; state is the result of projection, and time
      is one coordinate among many.
    </p>

    <p>
      SSCCS is built by the <a href={site.axioms}>{site.organization}</a> under an open-core model,
      guided by its <a href={site.direction}>operational direction</a> and{' '}
      <a href={site.philosophy}>philosophy</a>. The stack spans the full pipeline, from formal
      specifications, through a software compiler toolchain, to an open hardware architecture. The
      model is actively materialising on the engineering frontier of the current silicon paradigm
      through{' '}
      <a href={`${site.projects}#recursive-synergy-of-the-shared-substrate`}>
        domain instantiations
      </a>{' '}
      built on three core infrastructure pillars:{' '}
      <a href="https://docs.ssccs.org/projects/syntagma">synTagma</a>,{' '}
      <a href="https://docs.ssccs.org/projects/nexus">neXus</a>, and{' '}
      <a href="https://docs.ssccs.org/projects/kinetics">kineTics</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>

<style>
  /* The scene is held behind the opening block and bleeds past it on every side,
     so the model is present before the reader reaches the Model section. */
  .intro {
    position: relative;
  }

  .intro__body {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
  }

  /* The title carries the mark and the name on one centred line. The mark is
     clipped by its round frame, so the corners of the square drawing are cut by
     the circle rather than floating inside it. */
  .title-row {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 14px;
    margin-bottom: 26px;
  }

  .title-row__mark {
    display: block;
    width: 44px;
    height: 44px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 50%;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: var(--bg);
  }

  .title-row__mark img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .title-row {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 10px;
    }

    .title-row h1 {
      text-align: center;
    }
  }
</style>
